I always wanted to become a beast in  blood-borne but it wasn't possible even  if I fill the beast meter to 100%  however with the old hunters expansion  turning into a beast is finally possible  here's a quick guide on how I got the  beast embrace rune which allows you to  turn into a beast  first and foremost make your way to the  hunters nightmare once you've arrived in  the hunters nightmare proceed until you  can enter the cathedral where you fought  vicar Amelia you'll notice there's a  cleric beast as glowing in flames laying  on an altar pick up the eye pendant from  him which will be used later to get into  the research halls make your way to the  first boss Ludwig and defeat them after  defeating Ludwig proceed past him until  you reach some stairs I will lead to two  members of the healing Church defeat  them both and insert the eye pendant  into the dead body on the altar the  altar will then lift up towards the next  area after you make the top head back to  the hunter's dream once back at the  hunter's dream teleport to the  underground corpse pot once you arrive  there make your way back to where you  inserted the eye pendant you'll notice  that there's a new altar in place of the  altar you took up to the next area here  you'll pick up Lawrence's skull you find  out Lawrence was the first vicar of the  healing Church and that he became the  first cleric beast now make your way  back towards the Cathedral where the  Burning cleric beast was hanging out  defeat Lawrence the first vicar and  you'll receive the Beast embrace rune  head back to the hunter's dream and  equip the beasts embrace rune you'll  notice you've now turned into a beast if  you have them equip your beast claws and  become a killing machine while in beast  mode you'll be able to gain more damage  but you'll also take way more damage so  be careful the Beast claws also have  some new attacks now that you're in  beast form when the Beast claws are  tricked and gained a roar from your l2  you can do a flying attack that can  stagger your opponent for back stabs and  you can use your light and heavy attacks  complex of note you can also use normal  weapons in beastmode but you will not  charge your peace meters good luck with  your beastly adventures and stay tuned  advanced calm for continuing coverage of  blood-borne the old hunters  Oh
 

